※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=3006

※ A `foreach` binds a name the way `let` does and is written the way `let` is,
※ so the colon is always there.  Two spellings of one thing is what this
※ language does not have -- and after `while` it could not be optional anyway,
※ a name on its own followed by a colon being a condition with a body after it.

@[startup]
fn main() → u8:
    let found: mut u8 = 0u8
    foreach i = 0u8…3u8:
        found ← found + i
    found
